  {
    n: "7",
    title: "OS loader (EFI application)",
    body: "BL33, or the PC's UEFI firmware, runs an EFI application from the FAT EFI System Partition: shim and GRUB, systemd-boot or the Windows Boot Manager. With Secure Boot on, the firmware checks it against db and dbx first. It loads the kernel, an initramfs and the command line. Linux can skip this stage: with the EFI stub, the kernel image is itself a PE/COFF EFI application. U-Boot can also boot the kernel directly from a signed FIT image.",
  },
  {
    n: "8",
    title: "Kernel entry",
