---

<BaseLayout title="Hardware" toc>
  <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-1"><span class="text-accent-blue">$</span> dmesg | grep -i boot</p>
  <h1 class="glitch is-intro mb-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-text" data-text="Hardware">Hardware</h1>

  <!-- What is it? -->
  <div class="mb-10 rounded-xl bg-accent-green/15 p-5 sm:p-6">
    <h2 class="mb-1 text-sm font-bold text-brand-text">What is it?</h2>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-body">
      A cheat sheet on what a chip does between power-on and the OS: the TF-A secure boot chain on Arm, the hardware it
      relies on and how common chips compare, how PCs do the same with BIOS and UEFI, how the kernel boots, and how
      secure boot differs from measured boot.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ====== SECURE BOOT ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// power-on --&gt; chain of trust</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Anatomy of a secure boot">Anatomy of a secure boot</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      The{" "}
      <a href="https://trustedfirmware-a.readthedocs.io/en/latest/design/firmware-design.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Trusted Firmware-A (TF-A)</a>{" "}
      cold boot, from the reset vector in ROM to the OS: BL1 verifies BL2, then BL2 verifies every BL3x image.{" "}
      <strong class="text-brand-text">BL</strong> stands for Boot Loader stage.
    </p>

    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1040" class="soc-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[900px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="soc-uni-title soc-uni-desc">
        <title id="soc-uni-title">TF-A secure boot chain, the hardware it uses, and real chips that run it</title>
        <desc id="soc-uni-desc">On the left, a list of real chips and the boot stages they run, with TF-A stages highlighted. In the middle, cards for the CPU, PLL, watchdog, boot ROM, OTP fuses, crypto engine, Trusted SRAM, flash and DRAM, each with an arrow to the boot stage it serves. On the right, the Reset, BL1, BL2, BL31, BL32, BL33 spine. A verification-failure branch halts the SoC, a dashed line marks the secure/normal world boundary, and the operating system starts once BL33 runs.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="abig" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- top labels -->
        <text class="divider-label" x="24" y="40">This chain on real chips</text>
        <text class="divider-label" x="580" y="40">Hardware it relies on</text>
        <text class="divider-label" x="858" y="40">Boot execution chain</text>

        <!-- ===== Real chips panel ===== -->
        <rect x="24" y="74" width="520" height="350" rx="10" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1"/>
        <rect x="44" y="94" width="10" height="10" rx="2" fill="#0f6e56"/>
        <text class="ts" x="60" y="99" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#334155">TF-A stage</text>
        <rect x="144" y="94" width="10" height="10" rx="2" fill="#94a3b8"/>
        <text class="ts" x="160" y="99" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#334155">vendor or other firmware</text>
        {chainRows.map((r, i) => {
          const y = 140 + i * 38;
          return (
            <g>
              {i > 0 && <line x1="44" y1={y - 19} x2="524" y2={y - 19} stroke="#e2e8f0" stroke-width="1"/>}
              <a href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <text class="chain-name chain-link" x="44" y={y} dominant-baseline="central">{r.name}</text>
              </a>
              <text class="chain" x="232" y={y} dominant-baseline="central">
                {r.chain.map(([label, tfa], j) => (
                  <>
                    {j > 0 && <tspan class="sep">{"\u00a0-->\u00a0"}</tspan>}
                    <tspan class={tfa ? "tfa" : "ven"}>{label}</tspan>
                  </>
                ))}
              </text>
            </g>
          );
        })}
        <text class="ts" x="44" y="384" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569">Most SoCs replace BL1 with a vendor boot ROM that verifies the next</text>
        <text class="ts" x="44" y="402" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569">stage. TF-A's BL1 also runs, from flash, on Raspberry Pi 3 and HiKey.</text>

        <!-- ===== Boot spine ===== -->
        <g class="c-stage">
          <rect x="858" y="74" width="132" height="54" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="924" y="96" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Reset</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="113" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">power-on</text>
        </g>
        <g class="c-purple badge"><circle cx="978" cy="88" r="9"/><text class="ts" x="978" y="88" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">1</text></g>
        <line x1="924" y1="128" x2="924" y2="144" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-stage">
          <rect x="858" y="144" width="132" height="264" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="924" y="172" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL1</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="190" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Trusted ROM, EL3</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="212" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Brings up the</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="228" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">platform, then</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="244" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">loads, then</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="260" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">verifies BL2.</text>
        </g>
        <g class="c-purple badge"><circle cx="978" cy="158" r="9"/><text class="ts" x="978" y="158" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">2</text></g>
        <line x1="924" y1="408" x2="924" y2="424" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-stage">
          <rect x="858" y="424" width="132" height="194" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="924" y="452" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL2</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="470" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">SRAM, S-EL1 or EL3</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="492" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Inits DRAM, locks</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="508" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">TrustZone, loads</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="524" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">and verifies the</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="540" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL3x images.</text>
        </g>
        <g class="c-purple badge"><circle cx="978" cy="438" r="9"/><text class="ts" x="978" y="438" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">3</text></g>
        <line x1="924" y1="618" x2="924" y2="634" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-stage">
          <rect x="858" y="634" width="132" height="64" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="924" y="660" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL31</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="678" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">EL3 runtime</text>
        </g>
        <g class="c-purple badge"><circle cx="978" cy="648" r="9"/><text class="ts" x="978" y="648" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">4</text></g>
        <line x1="924" y1="698" x2="924" y2="714" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-stage">
          <rect x="858" y="714" width="132" height="64" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="5 3"/>
          <text class="th" x="924" y="740" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL32</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="758" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">optional</text>
        </g>
        <g class="c-purple badge"><circle cx="978" cy="728" r="9"/><text class="ts" x="978" y="728" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">5</text></g>
        <line x1="924" y1="778" x2="924" y2="800" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.4" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-stage">
          <rect x="858" y="800" width="132" height="54" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="924" y="820" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL33</text>
          <text class="ts" x="924" y="837" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">DRAM, EL2/EL1</text>
        </g>
        <g class="c-purple badge"><circle cx="978" cy="814" r="9"/><text class="ts" x="978" y="814" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">6</text></g>

        <!-- ===== Hardware / memory cards ===== -->
        <g class="c-gray"><rect x="580" y="74" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="95" dominant-baseline="central">CPU cluster</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="112" dominant-baseline="central">Arm cores; run every stage.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="101" x2="857" y2="101" stroke="#444441" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-gray"><rect x="580" y="144" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="165" dominant-baseline="central">PLL</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="182" dominant-baseline="central">Multiplies the crystal frequency.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="171" x2="857" y2="171" stroke="#444441" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-gray"><rect x="580" y="214" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="235" dominant-baseline="central">Watchdog</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="252" dominant-baseline="central">Resets the SoC if boot hangs.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="241" x2="857" y2="241" stroke="#444441" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-teal"><rect x="580" y="284" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="305" dominant-baseline="central">Boot ROM</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="322" dominant-baseline="central">Immutable first code; root of trust.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="311" x2="857" y2="311" stroke="#0f6e56" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-pink"><rect x="580" y="354" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="375" dominant-baseline="central">OTP / eFuses</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="392" dominant-baseline="central">Burned-in root-key hash + config.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="381" x2="857" y2="381" stroke="#993556" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-coral"><rect x="580" y="424" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="445" dominant-baseline="central">Crypto engine</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="462" dominant-baseline="central">Optional signature accelerator.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="451" x2="857" y2="451" stroke="#993c1d" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-teal"><rect x="580" y="494" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="515" dominant-baseline="central">Trusted SRAM</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="532" dominant-baseline="central">BL2 and BL31 run here; BL32 may too.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="521" x2="857" y2="521" stroke="#0f6e56" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-amber"><rect x="580" y="564" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="585" dominant-baseline="central">Flash storage (off-die)</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="602" dominant-baseline="central">Board chip; holds the FIP images.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="591" x2="857" y2="591" stroke="#854f0b" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <g class="c-blue"><rect x="580" y="800" width="250" height="54" rx="9" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="594" y="821" dominant-baseline="central">DRAM (off-die)</text>
          <text class="ts" x="594" y="838" dominant-baseline="central">Board memory; BL33 and OS run here.</text></g>
        <line x1="826" y1="827" x2="857" y2="827" stroke="#185fa5" stroke-width="2.6" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <!-- ===== Verification-failure branch ===== -->
        <g class="c-red"><rect x="598" y="650" width="214" height="60" rx="10" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="705" y="672" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Verification failed</text>
          <text class="ts" x="705" y="690" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Any BL check fails: halt or recover.</text></g>
        <path d="M858 392 L838 392 L838 670 L814 670" class="wire-fail" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>
        <path d="M858 590 L846 590 L846 690 L814 690" class="wire-fail" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>

        <!-- ===== Secure / normal boundary ===== -->
        <line x1="16" y1="779" x2="992" y2="779" class="divider"/>
        <text class="divider-label" x="844" y="772" text-anchor="end">&#8593; Secure world (EL3 / Secure-EL1)</text>
        <text class="divider-label" x="844" y="793" text-anchor="end">&#8595; Normal world (EL2 / EL1)</text>

        <!-- ===== OS world ===== -->
        <path d="M924 854 L924 878 L147 878 L147 933" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.4" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>
        <rect class="os-world" x="16" y="900" width="976" height="132" rx="14"/>
        <text class="divider-label" x="32" y="922">Operating system, normal world (loaded, and ideally verified, by BL33)</text>
        <g class="c-green"><rect x="40" y="945" width="215" height="66" rx="10" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="147" y="972" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">OS kernel</text>
          <text class="ts" x="147" y="992" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">takes control</text></g>
        <g class="c-amber"><rect x="280" y="945" width="215" height="66" rx="10" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="387" y="972" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Mount FS</text>
          <text class="ts" x="387" y="992" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">files appear</text></g>
        <g class="c-gray"><rect x="520" y="945" width="215" height="66" rx="10" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="627" y="972" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">init / systemd</text>
          <text class="ts" x="627" y="992" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">starts services</text></g>
        <g class="c-gray"><rect x="760" y="945" width="215" height="66" rx="10" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="867" y="972" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Shell / scripts</text>
          <text class="ts" x="867" y="992" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">bash, python&#8230;</text></g>
        <line x1="255" y1="978" x2="280" y2="978" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>
        <line x1="495" y1="978" x2="520" y2="978" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>
        <line x1="735" y1="978" x2="760" y2="978" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig)"/>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Numbered boxes are boot stages; coloured cards are hardware, with an arrow to the stage that uses each one. Chip
        names link to their TF-A platform pages and are compared in the table below.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h3 class="mb-4 mt-10 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">Step by step</h3>
    <ol class="space-y-3">
      {steps.map((s) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-white" style="background:#534AB7">{s.n}</span>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-brand-body"><strong class="text-brand-text">{s.title}.</strong> {s.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-brand-bg px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-muted">
      Details vary by platform. In hardware, the chain can still be bypassed through an open JTAG/SWD debug port,
      unprogrammed secure-boot fuses, or bugs in the ROM's USB/UART download modes, which boot-strap pins can select
      (as in{" "}
      <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250710125856/https://ktemkin.com/post/fusee_gelee/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Fusée Gelée</a>). Fault injection is behind most of the breaks in the table below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== REAL SILICON ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// under the microscope</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Secure boot hardware on real dies">Secure boot hardware on real dies</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      Neither chip runs TF-A, but their delayered dies show the blocks a boot relies on: boot ROM, OTP fuses and SRAM on
      the RP2350, flash and SRAM on the STM32L431.
    </p>

    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <!-- RP2350 -->
      <figure class="rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 520 456" class="soc-svg block h-auto w-full rounded-md" role="img" aria-label="Delayered Raspberry Pi RP2350 die with the OTP fuse array, the two SRAM banks, the boot ROM and the PLLs outlined">
          <a href="https://github.com/aedancullen/hacking-the-rp2350/blob/master/2_anti_fuse_fuse_club/block_04_fromgimp_scaled_4k.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <image href="/images/rp2350-die.jpg" x="0" y="0" width="520" height="456"/>
          </a>
          <g fill="none" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <g stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="4" opacity="0.85">
              <rect x="41"  y="41"  width="126" height="27"  rx="3"/>
              <rect x="40"  y="95"  width="90"  height="318" rx="3"/>
              <rect x="301" y="258" width="178" height="157" rx="3"/>
              <rect x="264" y="382" width="35"  height="33"  rx="3"/>
              <rect x="129" y="396" width="55"  height="19"  rx="3"/>
            </g>
            <rect x="41"  y="41"  width="126" height="27"  rx="3" stroke="#993556" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="40"  y="95"  width="90"  height="318" rx="3" stroke="#0f6e56" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="301" y="258" width="178" height="157" rx="3" stroke="#0f6e56" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="264" y="382" width="35"  height="33"  rx="3" stroke="#0f6e56" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="129" y="396" width="55"  height="19"  rx="3" stroke="#5f5e5a" stroke-width="2"/>
          </g>
          <g class="die-pill">
            <rect x="41"  y="72"  width="66" height="15" rx="7" fill="#993556"/><text x="74"  y="80">OTP fuses</text>
            <rect x="46"  y="101" width="40" height="15" rx="7" fill="#0f6e56"/><text x="66"  y="109">SRAM</text>
            <rect x="307" y="264" width="40" height="15" rx="7" fill="#0f6e56"/><text x="327" y="272">SRAM</text>
            <rect x="202" y="391" width="56" height="15" rx="7" fill="#0f6e56"/><text x="230" y="399">Boot ROM</text>
            <rect x="133" y="378" width="34" height="15" rx="7" fill="#5f5e5a"/><text x="150" y="386">PLLs</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
          <strong class="text-brand-text">Raspberry Pi RP2350</strong> (Cortex-M33). The boot ROM checks a signed image
          from external flash against a key hash in the OTP fuses; the cores sit in the unlabelled logic. Outlines from
          Aedan Cullen's{" "}
          <a href="https://media.ccc.de/v/38c3-hacking-the-rp2350" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>38C3 talk</a>{" "}
          annotation. Photo:{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/aedancullen/hacking-the-rp2350" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Aedan Cullen</a>,{" "}
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>CC BY 4.0</a>.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <!-- STM32L431 -->
      <figure class="rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4">
        <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250708134934/https://serd.es/assets/stm32l431-floorplan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="block">
          <img src="/images/stm32l431-floorplan.jpg" width="1400" height="1391" loading="lazy" class="h-auto w-full rounded-md" alt="Delayered STM32L431 die with Flash 1, Flash 2, the flash high-voltage block, SRAM1, SRAM2, small SRAMs A to D and a large-cell library region outlined in red"/>
        </a>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
          <strong class="text-brand-text">ST STM32L431</strong> (Cortex-M4). No secure boot in ROM: just a factory
          bootloader in a system-memory region inside the flash. The uniform area is the logic, the irregular south edge
          is analog. Photo and annotations: Andrew Zonenberg's{" "}
          <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250513070742/https://serd.es/2025/01/02/STM32L431-teardown.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>teardown</a>{" "}
          (archived),{" "}
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.
