              <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">{what}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{bios}</td>
              <td class="py-2">{uefi}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-brand-muted">
      Sources:{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.osdev.org/MBR_(x86)" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>MBR (x86)</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/manufacture/desktop/windows-and-gpt-faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Windows and GPT FAQ</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/efi-stub.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>EFI boot stub</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://www.tianocore.org/tianocore-wiki.github.io/development/design-architecture/pi_boot_flow.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>PI boot flow</a>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">Secure Boot keys</h3>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-brand-body">
      UEFI Secure Boot continues the chain past the firmware: four key databases decide which OS loader may run.
    </p>
    <dl class="mb-4 grid gap-y-3 text-sm">
      {sbKeys.map(([abbr, name, body]) => (
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
