        <text class="ts" x="484" y="420" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">optional check</text>
        <line x1="600" y1="420" x2="634" y2="420" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig5)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="644" y="420" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">boot order</text>
        <line x1="740" y1="420" x2="774" y2="420" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 3" marker-end="url(#abig5)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="784" y="420" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">skips the OS loader</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        A Linux distribution under Secure Boot, on a PC or an Arm board with UEFI. Windows replaces shim and GRUB with
        its Boot Manager and winload, which check the kernel. Sources:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/rhboot/shim" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>shim</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/efi-stub.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>EFI boot stub</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.u-boot.org/en/latest/usage/fit/signature.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>U-Boot FIT signature</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/module-signing.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>module signing</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/device-mapper/verity.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>dm-verity</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h3 class="mb-4 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">Kernel boot, step by step</h3>
    <ol class="mb-4 space-y-3">
      {kernelSteps.map((s) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-white" style="background:#534AB7">{s.n}</span>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-brand-body"><strong class="text-brand-text">{s.title}.</strong> {s.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-brand-muted">
      Numbers continue the TF-A steps 0 to 6. Sources:{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/arch/arm64/booting.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Booting AArch64 Linux</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/efi-stub.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>EFI boot stub</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/ramfs-rootfs-initramfs.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>initramfs</a>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">Linux under Secure Boot</h3>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-brand-body">
      Microsoft signs{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/rhboot/shim" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>shim</a>, a small
      first-stage loader, with its UEFI CA. shim carries the distribution's certificate and checks GRUB and the kernel
      against it, or against a Machine Owner Key (MOK) that the user enrolls. GRUB's config file is not signed, which is
      what BootHole exploited. Since then, shim checks{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/rhboot/shim/blob/main/SBAT.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>SBAT</a>{" "}
      generation numbers in signed metadata, so a vulnerable version can be revoked by number instead of filling dbx
      with hashes. With{" "}
      <a href="https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/kernel_lockdown.7.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>kernel lockdown</a>{" "}
      on, which distributions usually enable under Secure Boot, the kernel loads only signed modules and also refuses /dev/mem, kexec of unsigned kernels and unencrypted hibernation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== SECURE VS MEASURED ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// verify vs record</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Secure boot vs measured boot">Secure boot vs measured boot</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      Two mechanisms run along the whole chain, from the root of trust to the kernel, on Arm and PCs alike. Secure boot (then trusted boot, in Windows terms) verifies each stage and
      stops on a bad signature. Measured boot hashes each stage into a TPM and never blocks, so a key store or a remote
      server can tell what actually ran.
    </p>

    <figure class="mb-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 550" class="soc-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[800px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="mb-title mb-desc">
        <title id="mb-title">Secure boot, trusted boot and measured boot on one boot chain</title>
        <desc id="mb-desc">A row of boot stages: BL1, BL2, BL31 and BL32, BL33, the OS loader and the kernel. Red arrows above the row show which stage verifies which: a root key hash anchors BL1, BL1 verifies BL2, BL2 verifies BL31, BL32 and BL33, BL33 verifies the OS loader (secure boot), and the OS loader verifies the kernel (Windows trusted boot). Indigo arrows below show BL1, BL2, BL33 and the OS loader hashing the next stage into a TPM, whose measurements feed local policy such as disk key unsealing and remote attestation.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="abig2" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="10" y="200" width="130" height="60" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="75" y="223" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL1</text>
          <text class="ts" x="75" y="242" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Boot ROM</text></g>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="180" y="200" width="130" height="60" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="245" y="223" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL2</text>
          <text class="ts" x="245" y="242" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">loads the rest</text></g>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="350" y="200" width="130" height="60" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="415" y="223" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL31 / BL32</text>
          <text class="ts" x="415" y="242" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">EL3 + secure OS</text></g>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="520" y="200" width="130" height="60" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="585" y="223" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">BL33</text>
          <text class="ts" x="585" y="242" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">U-Boot or UEFI</text></g>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="690" y="200" width="130" height="60" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="755" y="223" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">OS loader</text>
          <text class="ts" x="755" y="242" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">bootmgr, GRUB</text></g>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="860" y="200" width="130" height="60" rx="10" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <text class="th" x="925" y="223" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Kernel</text>
          <text class="ts" x="925" y="242" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">drivers, ELAM</text></g>
        <line x1="140" y1="230" x2="178" y2="230" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <line x1="310" y1="230" x2="348" y2="230" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <line x1="480" y1="230" x2="518" y2="230" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <line x1="650" y1="230" x2="688" y2="230" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <line x1="820" y1="230" x2="858" y2="230" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>

        <!-- verification lane (secure boot, then trusted boot) -->
        <g class="c-red"><rect x="10" y="40" width="130" height="44" rx="10" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="75" y="55" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Root key hash</text>
          <text class="ts" x="75" y="73" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">OTP or ROM</text></g>
        <line x1="45" y1="84" x2="45" y2="198" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <path d="M105 200 L105 160 L215 160 L215 198" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="160" y="148" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#791f1f" style="font-size:11px">verifies BL2</text>
        <path d="M275 200 L275 160 L385 160 L385 198" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="330" y="148" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#791f1f" style="font-size:11px">verifies BL31/32</text>
        <path d="M240 200 L240 130 L555 130 L555 198" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="397" y="118" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#791f1f" style="font-size:11px">verifies BL33</text>
        <path d="M615 200 L615 160 L725 160 L725 198" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="670" y="148" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#791f1f" style="font-size:11px">verifies OS loader</text>
        <path d="M785 200 L785 160 L895 160 L895 198" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="840" y="148" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#791f1f" style="font-size:11px">verifies kernel</text>
        <path d="M170 98 L170 90 L735 90 L735 98" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"/>
        <text class="th" x="452" y="76" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#791f1f" style="font-size:12.5px">Secure boot (firmware; TF-A calls it Trusted Board Boot)</text>
        <path d="M770 98 L770 90 L910 90 L910 98" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"/>
        <text class="th" x="840" y="76" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#791f1f" style="font-size:12.5px">Trusted boot (Windows)</text>

        <!-- measurement lane (measured boot) -->
        <line x1="75" y1="260" x2="75" y2="338" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="82" y="299" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#3730a3" style="font-size:11px">hashes BL2</text>
        <line x1="245" y1="260" x2="245" y2="338" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="252" y="299" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#3730a3" style="font-size:11px">hashes BL3x</text>
        <line x1="585" y1="260" x2="585" y2="338" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="592" y="299" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#3730a3" style="font-size:11px">hashes OS loader</text>
        <line x1="755" y1="260" x2="755" y2="338" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="762" y="299" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#3730a3" style="font-size:11px">hashes kernel, drivers</text>
        <g class="c-ind"><rect x="10" y="340" width="980" height="56" rx="10" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text class="th" x="500" y="361" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">TPM / secure element</text>
          <text class="ts" x="500" y="380" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Extend-only PCRs: new PCR = hash(old PCR + measurement), plus an event log. Nothing is blocked.</text></g>
        <line x1="250" y1="396" x2="250" y2="438" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <line x1="750" y1="396" x2="750" y2="438" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="10" y="440" width="480" height="56" rx="10" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text class="th" x="250" y="461" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Local policy</text>
          <text class="ts" x="250" y="480" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Unseal the disk key only if the PCRs match</text></g>
        <g class="c-stage"><rect x="510" y="440" width="480" height="56" rx="10" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text class="th" x="750" y="461" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">Remote attestation</text>
          <text class="ts" x="750" y="480" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">A signed PCR quote tells a server what booted</text></g>

        <!-- legend -->
        <line x1="10" y1="528" x2="44" y2="528" stroke="#a32d2d" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="54" y="528" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">verify: a bad signature stops the boot</text>
        <line x1="360" y1="528" x2="394" y2="528" stroke="#3730a3" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="404" y="528" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">measure: record a hash, never block</text>
        <line x1="700" y1="528" x2="734" y2="528" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#abig2)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="744" y="528" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">boot order</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Red arrows verify and can stop the boot. Indigo arrows only record. BL31 and BL32 verify nothing here and are
        measured by BL2; BL1 is the root of trust for measurement, so nothing measures it.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mb-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-brand-border text-left text-brand-text">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold"></th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Secure + trusted boot</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Measured boot</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="align-top text-brand-body">
          <tr class="border-b border-brand-border/60">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">Does</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">verifies a signature</td>
            <td class="py-2">hashes the image, extends a PCR</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-brand-border/60">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">On mismatch</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">halts or recovers</td>
            <td class="py-2">boots on, the PCR differs</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-brand-border/60">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">Answers</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">may this code run?</td>
            <td class="py-2">what code did run?</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-brand-border/60">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">Trust anchor</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">key hash in OTP or ROM</td>
            <td class="py-2">immutable ROM + TPM</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">Used for</td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">blocking unsigned code</td>
            <td class="py-2">key release, attestation</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-brand-bg px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-muted">
      <strong class="text-brand-text">Naming.</strong> Windows splits verification in two: secure boot (UEFI checks the
      OS loader) and &ldquo;trusted boot&rdquo; (the OS loader checks the kernel, drivers and ELAM). TF-A&rsquo;s
      &ldquo;Trusted Board Boot&rdquo; is the firmware half. Measured boot is separate: it records and never verifies,
      though some documents (Intel&rsquo;s tboot) also call it &ldquo;trusted boot&rdquo;. TF-A builds both with{" "}
      <code class="font-mono text-xs">TRUSTED_BOARD_BOOT=1</code> and <code class="font-mono text-xs">MEASURED_BOOT=1</code>.
      Sources:{" "}
      <a href="https://tf-a.docs.trustedfirmware.org/en/latest/design_documents/measured_boot.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>TF-A Measured Boot design</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/operating-system-security/system-security/secure-the-windows-10-boot-process" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Windows boot process</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
